1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:01,533
(Man:)As a matter of fact I do.

2
00:00:01,538 --> 00:00:05,138
(Man:)At a little place
called the DMV.

3
00:00:06,543 --> 00:00:07,673
(Raj:)He's got him there.

4
00:00:07,677 --> 00:00:11,277
(Raj:)The D even stands
for department.

5
00:00:11,281 --> 00:00:12,481
Excuse me!

6
00:00:12,482 --> 00:00:13,582
(Sheldon:)Excuse me,
can I please

7
00:00:13,583 --> 00:00:14,983
(Sheldon:)see a show of hands?

8
00:00:14,985 --> 00:00:17,615
(Sheldon:)Who here takes issue with
this person cutting the line?

9
00:00:19,389 --> 00:00:21,859
(Man:)Told you.

10
00:00:21,858 --> 00:00:24,128
(Sheldon:)Well, what a sad
state of affairs!

11
00:00:24,127 --> 00:00:25,997
(Sheldon:)That you've all been
so ground down

12
00:00:25,996 --> 00:00:28,626
(Sheldon:)by life, you don't even notice
when someone disrespects you.

13
00:00:28,632 --> 00:00:30,262
(Howard:)I can't believe
we're gonna get beat up,

14
00:00:30,267 --> 00:00:33,837
(Howard:)and it's not
because of your chair.

15
00:00:33,837 --> 00:00:36,137
(Sheldon:)You know, right now,
at the back of this line,

16
00:00:36,139 --> 00:00:37,809
(Sheldon:)there's a movie fan
like you

17
00:00:37,808 --> 00:00:39,238
(Sheldon:)who's not going to get in,

18
00:00:39,242 --> 00:00:41,612
(Sheldon:)because this person
simply doesn't care.

19
00:00:41,611 --> 00:00:43,081
(Sheldon:)Yeah, well, 61 years ago,

20
00:00:43,079 --> 00:00:45,209
(Sheldon:)there was another person
at the back of the line

21
00:00:45,215 --> 00:00:47,515
(Sheldon:)and her name
was Rosa Parks.

22
00:00:50,587 --> 00:00:52,817
(Leonard:)Okay, you may have
to pretend you're black

23
00:00:52,823 --> 00:00:56,053
(Leonard:)to get us out of here.

24
00:00:56,059 --> 00:00:58,529
(Sheldon:)Now, let's follow in that
brave woman's footsteps,

25
00:00:58,528 --> 00:01:00,828
and stand up for ourselves!

